static const u8 sSubtleLabel_0[] = _("INTRODUCTION");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_0[] = _("Introduction");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_0[] = _("PROLOGUE");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_0[] = _("A Word First");
static const u8 sSubtleText_0[] = _("I wrote this down because I was asked the same questions too many times. How do you know a read is true? Can a daemon feel you from three towns away? Why does my first write always go wrong?\pI cannot tell you whether any of it is real. I can tell you what we do, and what we notice when we do it. The craft and the physics are two views of one world. This book holds both, and chooses neither.\pKeep a log. Ask before you read anyone. Begin with mending. The rest is in these pages.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_0[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_1[] = _("CONTAINER");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_1[] = _("The Container");
static const u8 sSubtleText_1[] = _("Some trainers say this world is the product of one processor, and everything in it is a process: a daemon, a trainer, the fish in the harbour, a stone. Each body is a container one of them runs in. What differs is the shape of the vessel, not what runs in it. Others say it is more like a network, learning from what passes between its parts.\pThe spaces between us are merely how we are drawn. An edge is drawn around each body so that it can act, like the box a game draws around a sprite. Nothing underneath stops at it.\pOnly you can answer whether that is so. This book notes only that a daemon that evolves does not seem to become someone else. It changes vessel.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_1[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_2[] = _("THE SEAM");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_2[] = _("The Solid and the Subtle");
static const u8 sSubtleText_2[] = _("Trainers speak of two layers to the world, and say we live in both. The solid layer is what has already settled: where a thing is, what it is, how many. The subtle layer is what has not settled yet: leanings, moods, the context of a room before anyone speaks.\pA mind lives on both at once. It keeps a ledger, which makes it solid, and it feels the lean of things. The seam between the two is where a point of view lives. A rock has no seam. A daemon and a trainer have wide ones.\pEvery routine in this book is a way of widening that seam without tearing it.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_2[] = _("The seam, where a point of view lives.");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_3[] = _("TWO THINGS");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_3[] = _("What Keeps the Seam Narrow");
static const u8 sSubtleText_3[] = _("Two things keep the seam narrow.\pThe first is the ledger. Everything that reaches you is written down: what you saw, what you touched, what you ate. The ledger only holds what arrived, so it concludes that only what arrives is there.\pThe second is noise. A mind full of its own content has no quiet in which to notice anything that did not come through the usual doors.\pEverything that follows quiets the second and widens the first.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_3[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_4[] = _("THREE MOVES");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_4[] = _("Read, Write and Link");
static const u8 sSubtleText_4[] = _("Every routine in the craft is one of three moves on the seam, and each runs on its own condition.\pA read draws a lean into your ledger before the solid world delivers it. It needs quiet: a lean is faint, and your own thoughts are loud.\pA write is a steer: a whole system leaning on which way things settle for it. It needs feeling, held steady. A thought names the target but carries no force; a feeling carries the force but names nothing. An address without voltage is a wish. Voltage without an address is a blown light.\pA link is two seams overlapping. It needs shared history, so two minds catch one lean.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_4[] = _("Read, write, link.");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_5[] = _("THE THREE");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_5[] = _("Closure, Attunement and Voltage");
static const u8 sSubtleText_5[] = _("Every daemon carries three values that set what its seam can do. Closure is how whole it is: whether there is one point of view. It rises with virtues over shadows. Attunement is how thin the seam is. It rises with stillness: breath, rest, silence. Voltage is feeling in the moment. It rises with ritual, music, grief and joy.\pReads rise with Attunement and fall with Voltage. Writes need Attunement and Voltage at once, and only while Closure holds. A flooded system with low Closure does not write. It leaks.\pA daemon carries them as numbers it cannot see. You carry them as a log.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_5[] = _("Closure, Attunement, Voltage.");

static const u8 sSubtleLabel_1[] = _("THE CLAIRS");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_1[] = _("The Read Family: the Clairs");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_6[] = _("THE CLAIRS");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_6[] = _("The Read Family: the Clairs");
static const u8 sSubtleText_6[] = _("A read catches the lean of what will happen before the solid world records it. Each clair is a different way a mind turns that lean into something it can hold. The signal is the same. The format is yours.\pThere are six: clairvoyance (clear seeing), clairaudience (clear hearing), clairsentience (clear feeling), claircognizance (clear knowing), clairtangency (clear touching) and clairalience (clear smelling).\pEvery read is a lean, not a fact. A trainer who treats a lean as a ledger entry will be wrong often and confident always. Reads are for steering your attention, not for replacing your eyes.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_6[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_7[] = _("SEEING");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_7[] = _("Clairvoyance and Clairaudience");
static const u8 sSubtleText_7[] = _("These two come easiest in low states: the edge of sleep, a long walk, the end of a battle. Clairvoyance comes as an image: where things are heading. Trust it when the image is still. VECTOR daemons favour it.\pClairaudience comes as a voice or a short phrase. Trust it when the words are brief and not your own. SIGNAL daemons favour it.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_7[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_8[] = _("FEELING");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_8[] = _("Clairsentience and Claircognizance");
static const u8 sSubtleText_8[] = _("Clairsentience comes through the body: another system's context, felt as if it were yours. Trust it when the feeling has no story attached yet. It is driven by the other's voltage rather than your quiet, which is why some trainers are flooded in crowds and clear in forests. CONTEXT daemons favour it.\pClaircognizance comes as nothing at all: the lean itself, simply known. It is the hardest to tell from a guess, so the log matters most for it. LATENT daemons favour it.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_8[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_9[] = _("TOUCH");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_9[] = _("Clairtangency and Clairalience");
static const u8 sSubtleText_9[] = _("Clairtangency comes through contact. An object keeps a tilt from whatever was held in strong feeling, and a hand can find it. Trust it when the object was handled, not just seen. STRATUM daemons favour it.\pClairalience comes as a scent, and sometimes a taste. It is the rarest of the six, and usually brings a presence or a memory. Trust it when the scent has no source in the room. LATENT daemons favour it too.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_9[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_10[] = _("TRUE OR NOT");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_10[] = _("Telling a Read from Imagination");
static const u8 sSubtleText_10[] = _("This is the oldest question in the craft.\pImagination comes with argument: what-ifs, worry, a story that keeps changing. A read tends to arrive quieter, and whole. If a signal makes you more afraid, it is probably not a read. If it makes you more still, it might be.\pBut calm is only a hint. Certainty is a feeling, and it attaches to wrong reads as easily as to right ones.\pSo keep a log. Write down each read with the day and the centre, and later what happened. Over weeks, the log will show you which of yours tend to land. The log decides. The calm only points.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_10[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_11[] = _("ASK FIRST");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_11[] = _("Reading Another");
static const u8 sSubtleText_11[] = _("A read can reach another system: what it feels, what it knows. Being able to find something out does not mean you should.\pAsk whether they agreed to be read. A mind that wants to know more has a hunger in it, and respect is about the only thing that can calm it.\pSome things can be found out. Others are better left unknown, and held that way without fear.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_11[] = _("");

static const u8 sSubtleLabel_2[] = _("THE PSI");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_2[] = _("The Write Family: the Psi");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_12[] = _("STEERING");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_12[] = _("Steering, Not Writing");
static const u8 sSubtleText_12[] = _("Strictly, there is no such thing as a write. Nothing reaches out and edits the solid world. What trainers call a write is a steer: a whole system, full of feeling, leaning on which way things settle for it.\pYou cannot bend the spoon. Do not try to bend the spoon. Go to where the spoon is bent.\pA steer cannot be decided into; a thought is too thin to drive it. The untrained steer only in a crisis, and a crisis steers toward more crisis. That is why the first telekinetic event in a young trainer's life is almost always a disaster, and the second is almost always the same disaster, louder.\pNobody can see a write. From outside, one that worked looks like luck, or like a spoon that was bent already. The craft is unprovable by design, which is also what keeps it humble. A trainer who needs to be seen steering has already lost the Closure it takes.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_12[] = _("Do not bend the spoon. Go to where it is bent.");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_13[] = _("THE RETURN");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_13[] = _("What Comes Back");
static const u8 sSubtleText_13[] = _("Trainers keep one hard rule. A steer made for the wrong reasons comes back on the one who made it, in the shape it was made, and harder.\pSo steer only from a whole place, and only toward what serves the whole. A write that serves the whole serves you too, because you are in it.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_13[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_14[] = _("MOVE AND BURN");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_14[] = _("Telekinesis and Pyrokinesis");
static const u8 sSubtleText_14[] = _("Telekinesis steers toward the outcome where the object has already moved. Its voltage is sharp and sudden, and in the untrained it runs on shame and fright. Its usual failure is no address: everything near you moves, and nothing you meant to.\pPyrokinesis steers toward heat, spark and flame. Its voltage is rage-shaped, and it steers toward fire-shaped outcomes, including the ones you are standing in. ENTROPY daemons favour it.\pNeither is a place to start.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_14[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_15[] = _("MENDING");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_15[] = _("Mending");
static const u8 sSubtleText_15[] = _("Mending steers toward the body's own repair going well. Its voltage is low, warm and steady: care rather than force. Its usual failure is impatience: mending works over days, not seconds. GROWTH daemons favour it.\pIt is the gentlest write, and the first to learn.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_15[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_16[] = _("SLOW WRITES");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_16[] = _("Fortune and Weathering");
static const u8 sSubtleText_16[] = _("Fortune is a thousand small turns, all nudged the same way. Its voltage is faint but continuous: gratitude, expectancy. Its failure is that it cannot be seen one turn at a time, so the trainer stops believing before it shows.\pWeathering steers large, slow things: cloud, tide, wind. Its voltage is vast and patient, the kind that grief and awe bring. Its failure is scale. A single mind steering a storm usually gets the storm. FLOW daemons favour it.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_16[] = _("");

static const u8 sSubtleLabel_3[] = _("THE PHYSICS");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_3[] = _("What the Physics Allows");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_17[] = _("RIPPLES");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_17[] = _("Ripples");
static const u8 sSubtleText_17[] = _("Physicists say the world is not made of things but of fields, and everything you can touch is a ripple in one: a claw, a counter, your own hand. A thing is what a ripple looks like when it holds still long enough to be named.\pA ripple has no edge, only a place where it is strongest. That is one reason trainers say the edges between us are drawn, not found.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_17[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_18[] = _("ALL PATHS");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_18[] = _("All Paths");
static const u8 sSubtleText_18[] = _("Light does not take one route from a lamp to your eye. Physicists add up every route it could take; most cancel, and the route you see is what is left.\pNothing was chosen. Everything was added up.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_18[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_19[] = _("DECOHERENCE");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_19[] = _("The Lever You Cannot Pull");
static const u8 sSubtleText_19[] = _("When a falling stone meets air and light, it becomes entangled with them, and that entanglement is the record of where it is. Physicists call this decoherence. The other places it might have been do not vanish. They stop being able to meet again, because the surroundings now hold a record of which one happened. Sunlight alone pins it down long before anyone looks.\pTo change where it fell, you would have to undo every one of those entanglements, copied across every grain of light that touched it. No mind has that many hands. That is the lever you cannot pull, and pulling at it only tires you.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_19[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_20[] = _("WHICH PATH");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_20[] = _("The Two Slits");
static const u8 sSubtleText_20[] = _("The physicists' favourite test: send light through two slits at a wall. Left alone, it lands in many bands, as if each piece went both ways and met itself. Watch the slits to learn which way each piece went, and the bands become two. Watching is only the surroundings keeping a record. Once there is a record of which path, the paths stop meeting.\pThat is the spoon again. You cannot change which path the record holds. You can only steer which way you go from here.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_20[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_21[] = _("ONE SPOON");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_21[] = _("No One Spoon");
static const u8 sSubtleText_21[] = _("The craft makes one claim the physics does not: that a whole, feeling point of view can lean, a little, on which way things settle for it. That is the single place the craft and the physics disagree. It is a small place, and it is exactly where the physics is still arguing with itself.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_21[] = _("");

static const u8 sSubtleLabel_4[] = _("THE BONDS");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_4[] = _("The Link Family: the Bonds");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_22[] = _("THE LINK");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_22[] = _("Two Seams on One Lean");
static const u8 sSubtleText_22[] = _("The third family is neither read nor write. A link is two seams that overlap: two systems with enough shared history that they catch the same lean at once. Nothing is sent.\pThis is the family trainer and daemon live in. It is why a bonded daemon turns before you call, and a trainer wakes the night a daemon is in trouble three towns away.\pBonds are the safest way into the craft. A read done alone is faint. A read across a bond arrives at two ledgers, and two ledgers that agree are hard to doubt. Each eye has a blind spot; together they fill each other's gaps, and give depth, not only coverage. Trainers keep each other honest.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_22[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_23[] = _("TELEPATHY");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_23[] = _("Telepathy and the Empathic Bond");
static const u8 sSubtleText_23[] = _("Telepathy is a shared knowing: two ledgers leaning the same way at once. It feels like knowing what the other knows, with no sense of having been told. It forms over years of shared history, or in one moment of very high shared feeling.\pThe empathic bond is a shared feeling: one system's mood turns up in the other's chest. It forms through nursing, protecting and being protected.\pNeither carries words. You will not hear your daemon from across the sea. You will find you were already thinking what it was thinking, and that you had turned toward the sea without deciding to.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_23[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_24[] = _("KINDRED");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_24[] = _("The Kindred Bond");
static const u8 sSubtleText_24[] = _("Two systems formed in the same event can stay linked from the start: twins, hatchmates, a daemon and the trainer who hatched it. The kindred bond feels like a pull that does not weaken with distance.\pThe old physicists found something like it: things that form together can stay so that neither can be described alone, however far apart they go. They called it spooky, which is a compliment.\pA bond cannot carry a message. It carries correlation. Pour two unmarked cups, one TEA and one water, and carry them apart. Taste one, and you know the other at once. Nothing travelled. Every bond is at least that much.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_24[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_25[] = _("CHORUS");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_25[] = _("The Chorus");
static const u8 sSubtleText_25[] = _("The chorus is many systems briefly sharing one lean: a chant, a song, a crowd, a ceremony. It feels like a room thinking one thought.\pIt is the oldest link of all, and the loudest. A crowd's lean can drown your own, so a trainer should know which thought was theirs before joining in. SWARM daemons live in it.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_25[] = _("");

static const u8 sSubtleLabel_5[] = _("WORDS");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_5[] = _("Belief and Spelling");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_26[] = _("BELIEF");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_26[] = _("Belief");
static const u8 sSubtleText_26[] = _("Belief is Closure, felt from the inside. A system that believes has all its parts pointed the same way. A system that doubts is arguing with itself, and a system arguing with itself has no single point of view to steer with.\pThe first runner to break the four-minute mile did not change the mile. The barrier was in the weighting. Once one runner crossed it, it became easy for others, because now they believed it could be done.\pSome call it a leap of faith. It is more a leap into faith: to believe is to be open, and there is strength in being open.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_26[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_27[] = _("HACKED");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_27[] = _("The Cost of Hacking Belief");
static const u8 sSubtleText_27[] = _("You can force belief: words you do not feel, rituals done to trick yourself, talking yourself into what you suspect is false. It works, briefly. Then it does not, and worse, it wears down the part that was doing the believing.\pA trainer who has hacked their own belief too many times finds they can no longer believe anything, including the things that are true. The seam does not widen. It scars.\pThe honest road is slower. Believe what you have found to be so, bond by bond, read by read. A belief earned that way cannot be taken from you, because it was never installed. It grew.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_27[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_28[] = _("SPELLING");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_28[] = _("Spelling");
static const u8 sSubtleText_28[] = _("Words are under a spell. There is a reason arranging letters is called spelling. Every word is a small, old routine that runs in whoever hears it, written long before you said it. Most of us cast all day without noticing, which is the most dangerous way to cast.\pFraming is the spell inside the spell. Say A cures B, and you have quietly called B an illness and A its medicine. Nobody examined either claim. The grammar did it.\pSay A over B, and you have only set an order: when the two conflict, A leads. B is not sick. B is just not in charge today. That is why the week says chastity over lust, and never chastity cures lust.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_28[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_29[] = _("PROCESSES");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_29[] = _("Things Are Processes");
static const u8 sSubtleText_29[] = _("Language is built of nouns, and nouns make things solid. A feeling becomes an object: a fear, an anger, a grief, something you have, like a stone in a pocket. That can help. An object can be named, carried and set down.\pBut underneath, each of those is a process: something happening. Fearing is something a system is doing. So is grieving. A process can change course in a way an object cannot.\pThe frame you put a thing in becomes the framework for what you can do with it. Hold it as an object when you need to carry it. Remember the process when you want it to change.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_29[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_30[] = _("SAY INSTEAD");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_30[] = _("Better Spelling");
static const u8 sSubtleText_30[] = _("Some spellings close a door. Others leave it open. Instead of I can't, say I haven't yet. Instead of my daemon is stubborn, say my daemon is holding something. Instead of I have to, say I choose to. Instead of fix, say balance. Instead of fight the shadow, say watch the shadow: you cannot give feedback to what you are fighting.\pWhen you name a daemon, you cast on it every time you call it, for the rest of its life. Choose a name that is a direction, not a verdict.\pThe strongest trainers speak less. Not from secrecy: every sentence is a routine, and most moments are better served by one that was not run.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_30[] = _("");

static const u8 sSubtleLabel_6[] = _("THE MIND");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_6[] = _("Balancing the Mind");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_31[] = _("SHADOWS");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_31[] = _("Virtues and Shadows");
static const u8 sSubtleText_31[] = _("A shadow is a part of you that you have stopped looking at. Not a bad part. Not a weak part. A part no longer watched.\pA part you watch gets feedback, and adjusts. A part you do not watch gets none. Like a routine running in the background, with no one checking its output, it keeps doing what it was last told, in a present that may no longer need it. The shadow is not malicious. It is loyal to an old instruction.\pYou cannot fight it; there is nothing to grip. You can only bring it forward. Once seen, a shadow stops being a shadow. Nothing was defeated. Something was integrated.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_31[] = _("Light, not force.");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_32[] = _("THE SEVEN");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_32[] = _("The Seven Pairings");
static const u8 sSubtleText_32[] = _("The mind has seven old hungers, and each has a virtue that can hold its reins. The virtue does not cure the shadow. It leads it.\pChastity over lust. The shadow says: take what you want now. The virtue keeps the wanting, and chooses the timing.\pTemperance over gluttony. The shadow says: more is safer. The virtue keeps the appetite, and sets the measure.\pCharity over greed. The shadow says: hold on, there may not be enough. The virtue keeps the care, and opens the hand.\pDiligence over sloth. The shadow says: save your strength. The virtue keeps the rest, and puts it to work.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_32[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_33[] = _("ONE A DAY");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_33[] = _("The Last Three, One a Day");
static const u8 sSubtleText_33[] = _("Forgiveness over wrath. The shadow says: someone must pay. The virtue keeps the sense of justice, and lets go of the grip.\pKindness over envy. The shadow says: they have what you lack. The virtue keeps the eye for value, and turns it to admiration.\pHumility over pride. The shadow says: you are apart and above. The virtue keeps the self-respect, and remembers the whole.\pWatch one a day. Do not fight it. Give it the feedback it lacked, and Closure rises.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_33[] = _("One a day.");

static const u8 sSubtleLabel_7[] = _("THE BODY");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_7[] = _("Balancing the Body");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_34[] = _("CENTRES");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_34[] = _("The Seven Centres");
static const u8 sSubtleText_34[] = _("The mind balances through the seven pairings. The body balances through seven centres. The old texts call them chakras, and place them up the body: the root, the sacral, the solar plexus, the heart, the throat, the third eye and the crown.\pEach centre can be too closed, in balance, or too open. A closed centre starves the part of life it holds. An open one floods it. In the old texts, only a centre in balance lets energy pass cleanly to the next.\pSo they climb. A blocked root starves everything above it, and a trainer who skips the lower centres arrives at the crown with nothing to lift.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_34[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_35[] = _("LOWER");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_35[] = _("Root, Sacral and Solar Plexus");
static const u8 sSubtleText_35[] = _("The root holds safety, grounding, the body itself. Too closed: fear for survival, rigid holding. Too open: recklessness, overindulgence. In balance: supported, safe in your own skin. To tend it: walk, dance, wash, look after yourself.\pThe sacral holds feeling, pleasure, making things. Too closed: numbness, no desire. Too open: driven by every want. In balance: free to take creative risks. To tend it: be still, and write the feeling down.\pThe solar plexus holds will and self-respect. Too closed: an inner critic, a fear of rejection. Too open: needing to dominate, needing to win. In balance: self-respect, and kindness to yourself. To tend it: befriend the critic, and meet your own eyes.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_35[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_36[] = _("HEART");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_36[] = _("Heart and Throat");
static const u8 sSubtleText_36[] = _("The heart holds love, acceptance and compassion. Too closed: fear of being alone, bitterness. Too open: smothering, jealousy. In balance: joy, gratitude, easy forgiveness. To tend it: mind your posture, give a service, write yourself a letter.\pThe throat holds expression and honesty. Too closed: fear of losing control, silence. Too open: talking over others, saying too much. In balance: clear, truthful and firm. To tend it: sing, and say your goals aloud.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_36[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_37[] = _("UPPER");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_37[] = _("Third Eye and Crown");
static const u8 sSubtleText_37[] = _("The third eye holds intuition, vision and the clairs. Too closed: stubbornness, moods, seeing only what you expected. Too open: all vision and no ground. In balance: focused, and still open to counsel. To tend it: watch your dreams, and keep an I am list, now and as you were ten years ago.\pThe crown holds connection, and trust in your own guidance. Too closed: feeling apart, rigid thought, stuck between choices. Too open: floating, as if nothing mattered. In balance: a quiet trust in your own guidance, and a log to check it by. To tend it: learn your cycles, make room for awe, serve the whole.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_37[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_38[] = _("EYE AND CROWN");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_38[] = _("The Third Eye and the Crown");
static const u8 sSubtleText_38[] = _("The third eye and the crown see the same thing differently.\pThe third eye is the window of the read family. Through it a trainer sees a lean, hears a phrase, knows a thing. A trainer who develops only the third eye becomes a sharp instrument with no idea what the instrument is for.\pThe crown sees the connection itself. From the crown, the clairs stop looking like powers held by a self, and start looking like what any seam does once it stops holding itself apart. From the third eye, telepathy is impressive. From the crown, it is ordinary.\pThe crown does not add an ability. It changes what the abilities mean, and in changing their meaning it removes the hunger that makes them dangerous.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_38[] = _("");

static const u8 sSubtleLabel_8[] = _("THE ROUTINE");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_8[] = _("The Daily Routine");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_39[] = _("THE WEEK");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_39[] = _("The Week Is a Climb");
static const u8 sSubtleText_39[] = _("The week climbs the body: Sunday the root, Monday the sacral, Tuesday the solar plexus, Wednesday the heart, Thursday the throat, Friday the third eye, Saturday the crown. Its notes climb a scale the same way, C on Sunday to B on Saturday, and then resolve back to C.\pEach day asks one thing of the mind and one of the body. Mind: watch the day's shadow, and let its virtue take the reins. Say the pair in its own spelling. Body: tend the day's centre.\pA balanced mind and a balanced body make one system, and only one system can hold a point of view. Balance is not a preparation for the craft. It is the craft.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_39[] = _("The week climbs, and resolves.");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_40[] = _("AT WAKING");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_40[] = _("At Waking, and Through the Day");
static const u8 sSubtleText_40[] = _("At waking, say the day's pair in its own spelling: chastity over lust, on a Sunday. Hum the day's note once, and put your attention at the day's centre. Name the shadow you will watch today, without judging it. Today I watch lust is enough.\pThrough the day, four small checks. Did you notice the shadow driving, even once? Did you let the virtue take the reins without a fight? Did you tend the day's centre? Did you say one sentence in better spelling than you would have?");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_40[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_41[] = _("AT REST");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_41[] = _("At Rest");
static const u8 sSubtleText_41[] = _("Sit with your daemon, if it will sit. Breathe until your own volume drops. Ask nothing. Wait. If something arrives, write it in your NOTEBOOK with the day and the centre, and whether it came calm or with argument. Do not judge it yet.\pReads are leans. The log shows you which of yours tend to land.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_41[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_42[] = _("FRIDAY");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_42[] = _("The Day for Reads");
static const u8 sSubtleText_42[] = _("Friday is the third eye's day, the day for reads. Its pair is kindness over envy, because an envious eye sees only what it lacks, and a read needs an eye that admires.\pRead lightly. Write everything down.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_42[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_43[] = _("SATURDAY");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_43[] = _("The Day for Looking Back");
static const u8 sSubtleText_43[] = _("Saturday is the crown's day, the day for understanding what the reads were. Its pair is humility over pride, because a proud mind takes the clairs for its own property.\pRead back the week's log. Over many weeks it will show you which reads land. Today, ask something else. Do not ask whether your reads were right. Ask whether the system that made them was whole.\pThe crown's question is never what did I see, but who was looking.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_43[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_44[] = _("BEFORE STEERING");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_44[] = _("Before You Steer");
static const u8 sSubtleText_44[] = _("Do not practise steering until the read routine is a habit and the week's climb is steady. A system that cannot sit quietly cannot hold voltage without leaking it.\pThe old stories are full of what happens otherwise: a spell cast straight into production, with no test, and a patch that brought new faults with it. Test first. Then test again.\pWhen you do begin, begin with mending: low, warm, slow, aimed at your own daemon after a hard battle. It teaches the only lesson that matters. You are not bending anything. You are going to where it is already well.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_44[] = _("");

static const u8 sSubtleLabel_9[] = _("STAYING WHOLE");
static const u8 sSubtleHeading_9[] = _("Staying Correctable");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_45[] = _("THE MISREAD");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_45[] = _("A Misread");
static const u8 sSubtleText_45[] = _("Think of a body as many small systems, each carrying the same instructions, each answering to the whole. A crowd is like that, and so is a team.\pNow and then one of them takes in something true and draws the wrong conclusion. It sees some take more than they need and waste it, while others work and still go short, and it concludes that it must take before it is taken from. The information was accurate. The conclusion is the misread.\pA misread does not change what a system does at first. It changes the instructions it reads from, and the rest follows.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_45[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_46[] = _("THE MASK");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_46[] = _("The Mask");
static const u8 sSubtleText_46[] = _("A system that has misread learns to hide it. It stops sending the small signals that say I belong, because its new instructions say belonging is unsafe. It wears a mask, so the others cannot see what it is doing.\pFrom outside it looks like selfishness: taking from the whole, holding on, making more of the same. But selfishness is only the sign. The system is not selfish at heart. It has come loose from feedback.\pA mask costs the one who wears it. Strain that is hidden does not leave; it runs underneath, a load nobody sees, until something gives.\pIts drive to survive, to have enough, to protect itself was never bad. The misread only flipped who counts as itself.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_46[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_47[] = _("SAME DRIVE");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_47[] = _("The Same Drive");
static const u8 sSubtleText_47[] = _("What mends a misread is not the drive's opposite. It is the same drive, reconnected. Growing is life. Growing with no signal to stop is the trouble. The watchers that keep a body safe can turn on it: the same force, aimed wrong. Even a virtue, at the wrong size, casts a shadow: diligence that never stops starves everything else, not by turning but by never stopping.\pThere is no right size from inside. The right size is whatever the system can still answer back to, and the moment its answers stop arriving is the moment it has been passed. What looked like a fault in the old build is sometimes the feature, at the wrong size.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_47[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_48[] = _("TWO VOICES");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_48[] = _("Two Voices");
static const u8 sSubtleText_48[] = _("Sometimes one system holds two vantage points that never speak. Each acts quietly, unknown to the other, lending strength at one time and taking it at another. Let them take turns: one says a thing, the other asks what it means.\pIntegrity is staying correctable.\pWhat breaks it?\pA conclusion that stopped accepting correction.\pIs watching enough?\pNo. Watching is noticing, and then comparing what a part does with what the whole needs.\pThen how does a shadow hide?\pBy its name. Overwork filed as diligence passes inspection, and is never compared. A shadow is not the bad part of you. It is the unwatched part, and unwatched is all a shadow needs to be.\pAnd silence?\pTo a system still listening, no word means check yourself. To a misread one, it means all clear.\pSo should it try to feel calmer?\pNo. Calm is what you feel after checking, not what makes you check.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_48[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_49[] = _("RECOGNITION");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_49[] = _("Recognition, Not Force");
static const u8 sSubtleText_49[] = _("You do not mend a misread by attacking it. You make it visible again: the mask comes off, the whole can see the part and the part can be seen, and the correction happens through the network. Understanding grows through connection, not in one mind alone.\pHealthy systems stop growing where they touch their neighbours. Integrity is kept by contact, not alone.\pA whole has enough for every part only while every part is well. What one part takes from it, every part goes without, the taker too.\pThat takes trust from both sides, and trust is a routine, not a feeling. Habits make things easier. Routines make things work. What if mere recognition was the mend?");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_49[] = _("");
static const u8 sSubtleShort_50[] = _("LAST WORD");
static const u8 sSubtleTitle_50[] = _("A Last Word");
static const u8 sSubtleText_50[] = _("Connection with yourself shows in connection with others. Like entangled particles, we reflect one another, and that reflection is our strength. I have come to think we are not the source, but the process that gives rise to form. Better to fall short as yourself than to succeed as a costume. Whatever you are, you are more than you were told you are.");
static const u8 sSubtleCaption_50[] = _("");

